<TextPage lang="en" title="Privacy policy" otherHref="/privacy/" updated="Last updated: 8 November 2026">
  <p>
    This is about the <strong>Kastoria City Buses</strong> app for Android and iPhone, the official app of Astiko KTEL
    Kastorias, made by Kastoria Dev Core.
  </p>

  <h2>In short</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We don't collect personal data. There are no accounts, ads, analytics or tracking.</li>
    <li>Your location is used only on your phone, when you ask for it, and isn't sent anywhere.</li>
    <li>What the app keeps (favourite stops, settings) stays on your phone.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Location</h2>
  <p>
    The app asks for location access to show you the stops near you, the buses that take you where you want to go ("Where do
    you want to go?") and where you are on the map. Your position is worked out and used only on your device, only while the
    app is open, and is neither stored nor sent to us or anyone else. The permission is optional: without it the app works as
    usual, just without "near me".
  </p>

  <h2>What the app keeps on your phone</h2>
  <p>
    Your favourite stops, language, theme and voice announcement setting, and copies of the timetables and announcements so it
    works offline. They don't leave the device, and are removed when you uninstall the app. Voice announcements use your
    phone's own voice.
  </p>

  <h2>What the app connects to</h2>
  <p>To stay current, the app downloads:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>the timetables and stops, from GitHub Pages;</li>
    <li>where the buses are right now, from our server;</li>
    <li>the operator's announcements, from our server;</li>
    <li>the map: on Android from OpenStreetMap, on iPhone from Apple Maps.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Nothing about you or your location is sent in these requests. As with any internet connection, the server sees your IP
    address and the app's version, which providers may keep for a while in logs under their own policies. We don't use them to
    identify you.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>The app is suitable for all ages and collects no data from anyone, children included.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If anything in this policy changes, we'll write it here, with a new date.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>For questions about this policy, see the <a href="/en/support/">support</a> page.</p>
</TextPage>
